      "message": "Nit: this long series of assertions is not very easy to read, and the error messages aren\u0027t easy to interpret, either. (they\u0027ll just be \"was: true; expected: false; good luck figuring out what that means\"). Suggest:\n\n    private void checkUidNetworkingBlocked(bool expectBlocked, int uid, int rules, bool X, bool Y) {\n        String msg \u003d String.format(\"uid\u003d%d rule\u003d%d X\u003d%b X\u003d%b: expected %s, got %s\",\n                uid, rules, X, Y,\n                (expectBlocked ? \"BLOCKED\" : \"UNBLOCKED\"),\n                (expectBlocked ? \"UNBLOCKED : BLOCKED\");\n    }\n\nOptionally, the following might also improve readability (maybe, and assuming it works):\n\n    final boolean BLOCKED \u003d true;\n    final boolean UNBLOCKED \u003d false;  // Or use an enum, which has automatic toString methods.\n\n    class TestCase {\n        int a;\n        int b;\n        int c;\n        bool d;\n        bool e;\n        public TestCase(int a, int b, int c, bool, d, bool e) {\n            this.a \u003d a;\n            this.b \u003d b;\n            this.c \u003d c;\n            this.d \u003d d;\n            this.e \u003d e;\n       }\n    }\n\n    TestCase[] testCases \u003d new TestCase[]{\n        new TestCase(UNBLOCKED, SYSTEM_UID, RULE_NONE, true, true).\n        ...\n    };",
