      "writtenOn": "2018-09-27T02:38:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure I\u0027m reading this right, but ISTM that we\u0027re mocking out the code that calculates whether something is blocked. If that\u0027s true, then does that mean that if we introduce a bug into isUidNetworkingBlocked, then this test won\u0027t fail?\n\nIt looks like the version of isUidNetworkingBlocked that we\u0027re using here is the 4-arg version which is effectively a static function that uses no NPMS state. So can we use that function directly?",
